 `detail` is included when an additional explanation is available.

+## Canvas global regions endpoint
+
+`GET /canvas/regions-api` returns every enabled Canvas PageRegion for the active
+theme in one request. Drupal's configured URL language negotiation selects
+translated component inputs, so language-prefixed requests retain their prefix.
+Anonymous responses contain saved content; a bearer token with the Canvas
+preview scope receives valid PageRegion auto-saves when present.
+
+The response maps theme region machine names to structured render trees or
+`null`. Its `cacheability` object contains the complete Drupal cache tags,
+contexts, and maximum age for the returned region trees:
+
+```json
+{
+  "regions": {
+    "pre_header": { "element": "js-text", "props": { "text": "Notice" } },
+    "post_header": null
+  },
+  "cacheability": {
+    "tags": ["config:canvas.page_region.example.pre_header"],
+    "contexts": ["languages:language_interface", "oauth2_scopes", "theme"],
+    "maxAge": -1
+  },
+  "theme": "example"
+}
+```
+
 ## Known limitations

 - The rendered-content endpoint serves the default revision: an unpublished entity previews fully, but a published entity's forward
